<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 163 0 R
/E (Yes, it's normal. Getting older brings challenges that can catch us by surprise. Everyone faces them in different ways, and you can't avoid them. But you don't have to face them on your own. It's good that you reached out, and don't hesitate to seek professional help from a therapist.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
363 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 163 0 R
/E (What I can offer you is a formula from the Baal Shem Tov for dealing with just about everything that comes your way. It's a three-step process: Acceptance, Separation and Sweetening.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
364 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 163 0 R
/E (Let's take your situation. You're not as young as you used to be. Neither are your parents. You don't have the energy, stamina, and light-heartedness you had twenty years ago. It's frustrating.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
365 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 163 0 R
/E (Let's apply the three steps.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
366 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 163 0 R
/E (First comes Acceptance. Accept that you are getting older. This is where you are. You can't fight reality. You can't reverse it. You can't go back in time. You can't switch lives with somebody else.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
367 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 163 0 R
