371 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 163 0 R
/E (I'm at a stage in my life where nothing's wrong but I'm not handling it. I've hit fifty, my parents are getting older, and I've got less patience. I haven't fulfilled the dreams I thought I would reach by now, and I'm not settled in myself. Is this normal? What do I do to get through this? It's starting to really get me down.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [16]
>>
endobj
372 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 163 0 R
/E (Response:)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [17]
>>
endobj
373 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 163 0 R
/E (Question:)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [18]
>>
endobj
374 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 163 0 R
/E (You are who you are, where you are, right here, right now. You don't call the shots, G-d does. Accept it. That doesn't mean giving up. It means starting from where you are. Until you accept that, we can't move on.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [19]
>>
endobj
375 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 163 0 R
/E (Once you've accepted reality as it is, you need to shift your perspective on it. This is the second step: Separation. Separate the facts of your life from the story you're telling yourself about them. Drop your assumptions. You have defined getting older as a bad thing. Separate from that definition and see it for what it is: entering your next stage. You aren't falling, you are progressing.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [20]
>>
endobj
376 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 163 0 R
/E (That sets up the final step: Sweetening. Turn what seemed negative into a positive. The things going on in your life, even if they seem like obstacles, can become stepping stones. Getting older means engaging in life on a more mature level, experiencing things more deeply, appreciating what you once overlooked. You may not have achieved everything you dreamed of, but perhaps there are new dreams you never even thought of.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [21]
>>
endobj
377 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 163 0 R
/E (You are being invited to go deeper into life, to embrace a new level, to take a step up. Difficulties are not just interruptions to life, they can be invitations to growth. Don't avoid the challenge. Take it on, bring it in, let it transform you. Make the bitter sweet.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [22]
>>
endobj
378 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 163 0 R
/E (You need all three steps: acceptance, separation, sweetening. You can't jump to sweetening without accepting where you're at and reframing it. Each step takes time and work.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [23]
>>
endobj
379 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 163 0 R
/E (But it's worth it. Here's the message for someone hitting fifty: you're not getting older. You're getting sweeter.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [24]
>>
endobj
